//? Title: TEA: actual modular cycles, round trips and bit sensitivity
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The Tiny Encryption Algorithm mixes two32-bit words through32 dependent double
rounds. Actual schedule and intermediate half words expose the mechanism; the
original single-bit sensitivity experiment remains an illustrative property
test.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

All additions, subtractions and left shifts are uint32 modulo2^32. Each
encryption cycle increments sum by delta=0x9E3779B9, then updates left from
right/key0,1 and right from the new left/key2,3. Decryption starts
sum=0xC6EF3720 and reverses these dependent updates before subtracting delta.
Thirty-two cycles are64 half updates. A mean near32 flipped output bits for
one64-bit input cohort is illustrative diffusion, not evidence of cryptographic
security. TEA has equivalent-key and related-key weaknesses; later TEA variants
are distinct algorithms, not a blanket security fix.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tea_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/tea.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::tea_encrypt_trace({0, 0}, {0, 0, 0, 0});
    std::print("| actual cycle | schedule hex | words before | first updated half hex | words after |\n| " "---: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
        const auto &s = r.steps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {:08x} | `{}` | {:08x} | `{}` |\n", s.cycle, s.sum,
                   s.before, s.first_updated, s.after);
    }
    std::print("Zero-block/key vector {:08x} {:08x}.\n", r.value[0], r.value[1]);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual zero block and zero key");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual dependent half updates",
                                     r.half_updates));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Cipher {:08x} {:08x}", r.value[0],
                                     r.value[1]));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/tea_tiny.svg");
}
```
